<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- StormReportsInput — the SPC storm-reports verification controls: a card, one row per report type, and
     fill opacity. Reused in BOTH temporal windows: in the Past window it shows the replay day's reports, in
     the Now window today's — the VM keys the overlay to the active convective day, so the same controls
     serve both.

       ┌────────────────────────────────────────────┐
       │ 448 reports                                │   the card: total, which convective day,
       │ May 20, 2013 · 12Z-12Z                     │   and loading/failure in the footer
       └────────────────────────────────────────────┘
       ────────────────────────────────────────────────
       [x] ● Tornado                             42     ← one row per type: the toggle, the SPC dot
       [x] ● Wind                               310       colour, the name and that type's count,
       [x] ● Hail                                96       all as ONE object
       Opacity ──────●──────────────

     ⚠️ THE SWATCHES USED TO BE DRAWN TWICE. There was a toggle row (three checkboxes, each with a coloured
     dot and a name) and a separate Count row that repeated all three dots with numbers beside them — the
     same three colours and the same three types, listed twice, one row apart. Merging them is most of what
     this layout is: a type is one line, and its count sits on the line that switches it.

     ⚠️ THE CARD'S HEADLINE IS A TOTAL THE ROWS BELOW ALSO BREAK DOWN, which is a genuine redundancy and was
     chosen anyway — see the ⚠️ on the card region in StormReportsViewModel. If it ever reads as noise the
     honest fix is to drop the card, not to invent a different number for it.

     ⚠️ THE SECTION HEADING IS NOT HERE — each host window draws its own (PastCastTab / NowCastTab) above
     this control. The window owns its section structure; this is content. That is also why there is no
     divider in here.

     ⚠️ Opacity is DISABLED while every type is off (ViewModel.AnyShown): nothing is on the map, so there is
     nothing for it to act on. Same off-switch rule as the outlook's "None".

     ⚠️ THE COUNTS POPULATE WITH EVERY BOX UNCHECKED, which is the whole reason the card is worth having.
     The fetch used to be gated on something being shown, so the numbers sat at zero until you ticked a box
     — they read as broken data rather than as an empty filter. They describe the DAY now; the checkboxes
     only decide what is drawn, and the card's footer says "None shown" so a full count over an empty map
     cannot be mistaken for one.

     ⚠️ IN PASTCAST THEY POPULATE AFTER *LOAD*, NOT ON A DATE CHANGE. The VM keys off the LOADED replay
     window, not the pickers — between editing a date and pressing Load the two describe different days, and
     counting the pending one meant the card reported a day that was not on the map.

     A [label | control] grid, one row per field, matching the picker rows in the sections above. Bound to
     StormReportsViewModel. -->
<UserControl x:Class="Anvil.Controls.Composites.StormReportsInput"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
             xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
             mc:Ignorable="d">

    <Grid VerticalAlignment="Top">
        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- the card -->
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- rule -->
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- the three type rows + opacity -->
        </Grid.RowDefinitions>

        <!-- THE CARD, the same shape as the Timeframe and outlook cards in this window. Like the outlook's
             it is a RESULT — there is no action here, the dots appear as you switch types on — so it
             carries no button. -->
        <Border Grid.Row="0" CornerRadius="8" Padding="13,12"
                Background="{ThemeResource OverlayBarSurfaceHoverBrush}"
                BorderThickness="1"
                BorderBrush="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}">
            <StackPanel>
                <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.CardHeadline, Mode=OneWay}"
                           FontSize="15"
                           Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorPrimaryBrush}"/>
                <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.CardContext, Mode=OneWay}"
                           FontSize="13" Margin="0,4,0,0" TextWrapping="Wrap"
                           Visibility="{x:Bind HasText(ViewModel.CardContext), Mode=OneWay}"
                           Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"/>
                <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.CardFooter, Mode=OneWay}"
                           FontSize="11" Margin="0,6,0,0" TextWrapping="Wrap"
                           Visibility="{x:Bind HasText(ViewModel.CardFooter), Mode=OneWay}"
                           Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorTertiaryBrush}"/>
            </StackPanel>
        </Border>

        <Border Grid.Row="1" Height="1" Margin="0,14"
                Background="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}"/>

        <Grid Grid.Row="2" RowSpacing="9">
            <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- Tornado -->
                <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- Wind -->
                <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- Hail -->
                <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- Opacity -->
            </Grid.RowDefinitions>

            <!-- One row per type. The count is right-aligned in its own column so the three numbers form a
                 column of their own however long the names get.
                 ⚠️ The dot colours are the SPC report colours the map draws (storm-reports.js): tornado red,
                 wind blue, hail green. They are literals in both places — change one, change the other. -->
            <CheckBox Grid.Row="0" MinWidth="0" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                      IsEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.IsReady, Mode=OneWay}"
                      IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.ShowTornado, Mode=TwoWay}"
                      ToolTipService.ToolTip="Show tornado reports">
                <Grid ColumnSpacing="9" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch">
                    <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                    </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    <Border Grid.Column="0" Width="11" Height="11" CornerRadius="6"
                            Background="#E51919" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="1" Text="Tornado" FontSize="13" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="2" Text="{x:Bind Fmt(ViewModel.TornadoCount), Mode=OneWay}"
                               FontSize="13" FontWeight="SemiBold" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                </Grid>
            </CheckBox>

            <CheckBox Grid.Row="1" MinWidth="0" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                      IsEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.IsReady, Mode=OneWay}"
                      IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.ShowWind, Mode=TwoWay}"
                      ToolTipService.ToolTip="Show wind reports">
                <Grid ColumnSpacing="9" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch">
                    <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                    </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    <Border Grid.Column="0" Width="11" Height="11" CornerRadius="6"
                            Background="#1663D8" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="1" Text="Wind" FontSize="13" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="2" Text="{x:Bind Fmt(ViewModel.WindCount), Mode=OneWay}"
                               FontSize="13" FontWeight="SemiBold" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                </Grid>
            </CheckBox>

            <CheckBox Grid.Row="2" MinWidth="0" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                      IsEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.IsReady, Mode=OneWay}"
                      IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.ShowHail, Mode=TwoWay}"
                      ToolTipService.ToolTip="Show hail reports">
                <Grid ColumnSpacing="9" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch">
                    <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                    </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    <Border Grid.Column="0" Width="11" Height="11" CornerRadius="6"
                            Background="#18A020" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="1" Text="Hail" FontSize="13" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="2" Text="{x:Bind Fmt(ViewModel.HailCount), Mode=OneWay}"
                               FontSize="13" FontWeight="SemiBold" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                </Grid>
            </CheckBox>

            <Grid Grid.Row="3" ColumnSpacing="12" Margin="0,4,0,0">
                <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="60"/>
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Text="Opacity" Style="{StaticResource SettingsFieldLabelStyle}"/>
                <Slider Grid.Column="1"
                        HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                        IsEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.AnyShown, Mode=OneWay}"
                        Minimum="0" Maximum="1"
                        StepFrequency="0.05" SmallChange="0.05"
                        IsThumbToolTipEnabled="False"
                        VerticalAlignment="Center"
                        Value="{x:Bind ViewModel.Opacity, Mode=TwoWay}"
                        ToolTipService.ToolTip="Overall opacity of the storm-report dots"/>
            </Grid>
        </Grid>
    </Grid>
</UserControl>
